!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/meta-service.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/39/m/meta.tn"
@meta.doc:"""
  A meta layer declaring an interface as a namespace of methods, and an HTTP binding naming the method it
  serves. A method's request, error and reply records are slots typed `kind<record>`, the names of the record
  types, so a schema importing this one writes them by name (`request: place_order_request`); its response is any
  type, `type_kind`. `interface` maps method names to methods, so a binding's `method`, a slot typed
  `ref<method>`, reaches one by a qualified name (`method: orders.place_order`), and `bindings` maps names to
  bindings. `rpc_method` composes `method`, so an rpc interface's methods fill a `ref<method>` through their
  supertypes; `verb_interface` keys its methods by `verb_name`, an identifier family whose members are the verbs,
  a namespace's keys being names. A `header_set` holds its methods in a plain map, `{text => method}`, which no
  qualified name enters, and `header_sets` maps names to header sets. A namespace type declares only its facets,
  so a `service`, which has fields of its own beside its methods, is a record holding an `interface` in its
  `methods` field, and `services` maps names to services: a binding reaches a service's method through the
  record's field (`method: shop.orders.methods.place_order`). An entry built with a namespace type is a value,
  not a type, and a processor that binds binds each value of its map to a host class of its own: the records
  `method`, `rpc_method`, `binding`, `header_set` and `service`.
  """
!schema {
  method_name    => meta.identifier
  status_name    => meta.identifier
  method         => { request?: meta.kind<meta.record>  response?: meta.type_kind  errors?: [meta.kind<meta.record>]  replies?: {status_name => meta.kind<meta.record>} }
  rpc_method     => method & { idempotent?: meta.boolean }
  http_verb      => !meta.enum [GET POST]
  verb_name      => !meta.identifier_type { members: [GET POST] }
  interface      => !meta.namespace { key_type: method_name  value_type: method }
  rpc_interface  => !meta.namespace { key_type: method_name  value_type: rpc_method }
  verb_interface => !meta.namespace { key_type: verb_name  value_type: method }
  header_set     => { headers: {meta.text => method} }
  header_sets    => !meta.namespace { key_type: meta.identifier  value_type: header_set }
  service        => { extends?: [meta.identifier]  methods: interface }
  services       => !meta.namespace { key_type: meta.identifier  value_type: service }
  binding        => { method: meta.ref<method>  verb: http_verb  route: meta.text }
  bindings       => !meta.namespace { key_type: meta.identifier  value_type: binding }
}
